# Cloud Functions config (issue #101). Firebase Functions v2 loads dotenv/params
# from THIS directory (firebase.json sets functions.source = "functions") — NOT
# the repo-root .env. Copy to `functions/.env` (all environments) or
# `functions/.env.gaycruisebingo` (the per-project override, <projectId> from
# .firebaserc). Real .env files are gitignored; this template is committed.
#
# These are non-secret firebase-functions/params defineString values with safe
# defaults baked in — set them here only to override a default.

# From address for transactional email.
#
# MUST be an address on a domain VERIFIED in Resend. As of 2026-08-05 the only
# verified sending domain on the account is `mail.nathanpayne.com`, which is
# what the default below now uses (#633). Resend rejects a send from an
# unverified domain and functions/src/email.ts swallows that into a logged
# `false` (ADR 0001's never-throw contract), so a project that overrides this
# to an unverified address will see the same SILENT failure — nothing
# delivered, nothing surfacing except a function log. Confirm any override is
# on a verified domain before deploying it.
EMAIL_FROM=Gay Cruise Bingo <gaycruisebingo@mail.nathanpayne.com>

# Per-Edition overrides of EMAIL_FROM (#671), one per brand in the #608
# lexicon: gcb / vacay / fiveacross. ADR 0008 splits Firebase projects by
# COHORT, not by brand, so one project (e.g. `fiveacross`) can serve several
# brands, and EMAIL_FROM alone cannot express a per-brand sender. The daily
# email and admin digest resolve the Event's Edition from its host and look
# up the matching param below FIRST, falling back to EMAIL_FROM only when it
# is unset.
#
# DEFAULT EMPTY, same convention as EMAIL_REPLY_TO below, and for the same
# reason EMAIL_FROM itself must sit on a Resend-VERIFIED domain: an unset
# value here is the signal that the brand's domain is not verified yet, so
# the send falls back to EMAIL_FROM rather than handing Resend a From: it
# will reject (swallowed into a logged `false`, never thrown, per ADR 0001).
# Set the matching param, per project, only AFTER that brand's domain is
# verified in Resend — as of this writing none of gaycruisebingo.com,
# vacaybingo.com, or fiveacross.app are verified (only mail.nathanpayne.com
# is, per #633), so all three stay empty here until verification lands.
# Recommended values, from plans/daily-cards-wireframes.html §
# fx-email-registers-tri:
#
#   EMAIL_FROM_GCB=Gay Cruise Bingo <bingo@gaycruisebingo.com>
#   EMAIL_FROM_VACAY=Vacay Bingo <hello@vacaybingo.com>
#   EMAIL_FROM_FIVEACROSS=Five Across <hello@fiveacross.app>
#
# Every param declared in functions/src/params.ts needs its own assigned line
# in this file even when the value is empty — an omitted line, not an empty
# value, is what makes a non-interactive `firebase deploy` hang on a prompt
# (see scripts/e2e-functions-env.mjs's header comment, #724).
EMAIL_FROM_GCB=
EMAIL_FROM_VACAY=
EMAIL_FROM_FIVEACROSS=

# Address replies land in, applied to every transactional send (#616). Empty =
# no Reply-To header at all (the shipped default; unchanged behaviour). Kept
# separate from EMAIL_FROM because that must sit on a Resend-verified SENDING
# domain, while replies want a mailbox a human actually reads — on the Five
# Across deployment those are deliberately different hosts, because the Resend
# receiving side is disabled.
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=
# Shared-inbox recipient for the admin notification digest (comma-separated),
# UNIONED with the Event's own `admins` roster (#638). Empty = roster only.
#
# BOTH SOURCES ARE LIVE; this is not an either/or. The roster is the per-Event
# answer and needs no deploy to change, but it only yields an address for an
# admin whose Firebase Auth email is VERIFIED — so a brand-new Event, or an
# admin signed in with an unverified address, resolves to nobody. Setting a
# shared inbox here is what guarantees the digest reaches a human on every
# project, and it is the recommended setting for any deployment that actually
# wants moderation mail. A project that leaves BOTH empty queues alerts and
# sends nothing (logged, never lost — they drain once a recipient exists).
ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL=
# Base URL for the admin digest's Review-queue deep link, and the fallback
# origin for the daily email's Feed CTA, when an Event has no `hostnames`
# mapping (#616, #638). An Event WITH a canonical hostname uses that instead.
APP_BASE_URL=https://gaycruisebingo.com

# Public URL of the emailUnsubscribe endpoint (#616) — the target of every daily
# engagement email's visible Unsubscribe link and its List-Unsubscribe header.
#
# Neither this URL nor the raw Cloud Functions one is reachable by itself. Both
# hit the SAME backing Cloud Run service, and the gaycruisebingo GCP project
# enforces Domain Restricted Sharing (constraints/iam.allowedPolicyMemberDomains),
# which rejects granting `allUsers` the Cloud Run invoker role on that service
# either way — a Hosting rewrite forwards the unauthenticated request into the
# same invoker check, it does not bypass it. The endpoint only answers once
# scripts/set-email-unsubscribe-invoker.sh has disabled the invoker IAM check
# on the backing service (the same mechanism scripts/set-bug-report-invoker.sh
# already uses for submitBugReport, #158) — run it after EVERY Functions
# deploy; see docs/app/bug-reports.md § Repeat-deploy hardening and
# docs/app/phase-1-deploy.md § 1a-i.
#
# Given that, the default still goes through Firebase Hosting (firebase.json
# rewrites /unsubscribe to the emailUnsubscribe function) rather than the bare
# Cloud Functions URL — but that choice is cosmetic: a first-party
# gaycruisebingo.com link is better for deliverability and less phishing-shaped
# than a raw *.cloudfunctions.net URL in a List-Unsubscribe header.
#
# PER-PROJECT, and the default is NOT portable: it names the gaycruisebingo
# deployment's own hosted URL. A second Firebase project (ADR 0008) that leaves
# this unset mails unsubscribe links pointing at the FIRST project, whose
# `emailPrefs` collection holds no document or token for that participant — so
# every unsubscribe request is answered "that link is no longer valid" and the
# recipient cannot opt out at all. Set it here, per project, to that project's
# own canonical host plus /unsubscribe (the same rewrite ships from this same
# firebase.json, so it only needs that project's Hosting to be deployed):
#
#   https://<that project's canonical host>/unsubscribe
EMAIL_UNSUBSCRIBE_URL=https://gaycruisebingo.com/unsubscribe

# RESEND_API_KEY is NOT an env var — it is a Google Secret Manager secret
# (defineSecret), set with `firebase functions:secrets:set RESEND_API_KEY`
# (value from the 1Password item "Resend API Key (gaycruisebingo)"). Never put
# it in this file.

# App Check enforcement for the submitBugReport callable (issue #44). Default
# OFF: with it false, a missing App Check token is accepted (the callable still
# enforces Firebase Auth in application code). Set to true ONLY once App Check
# client registration + enforcement from #44 are live — then a request without a
# valid App Check token fails closed. Declaring it here (not just relying on the
# defineBoolean default) keeps a non-interactive `firebase deploy` from stopping
# during parameter resolution when it prompts for an unset param (#158).
BUG_REPORT_APP_CHECK=false

# Gate for the moderateProof (Cloud Vision) Storage trigger (issue #126).
# Default OFF (Cloud Vision is deferred). When off, moderateProof is NOT
# exported, so Firebase never validates or deploys it and the #101 notifiers
# deploy on their own. Unlike the params above, this must be honored at DEPLOY
# TRIGGER DISCOVERY (the point where Firebase decides which functions exist) —
# and firebase-tools does NOT load these .env files into the discovery
# subprocess (only into the deployed function's RUNTIME env, and into param
# resolution, both AFTER discovery). So functions/src/visionGate.ts reads this
# file itself at discovery (it runs with cwd = this dir); see that file and
# docs/app/phase-1-deploy.md. The region mismatch that used to block the enabled
# path is resolved — moderateProof is pinned to region us-east1 to match the
# default bucket (#132) — so only set this to true once the Cloud Vision API is
# enabled on the project, then redeploy --only functions.
ENABLE_VISION_MODERATION=false
